    "Offsets: r.offset(d) -> Profile grows by d (shrinks when negative): an outside corner is rounded with radius |d| about the old corner, an inside corner stays sharp, a corner with edges too short gets a smaller radius (Corner::Reduced), never a refusal. r.offset_miter(d) -> Region keeps every corner sharp, for more booleans.",
    "Corners: p.round_corners(r), p.chamfer_corners(d), p.round_corners_with(r, max_share, min_r) (a corner uses at most max_share of each edge; under min_r it stays sharp); the same on Region. Each gives a Profile whose corners list says Corner::Full, Corner::Reduced(r) or Corner::Sharp per corner, and counts() gives [full, reduced, sharp].",
    "Output for extrude: poly.to_loop() and profile.to_loop() give one loop; region.to_loops() and profile.to_loops() give one loops array per separate piece (its outline, then its holes): one extrude each. profile.to_region(tol) splits arcs into edges for more booleans; profile.area() counts arcs exactly.",
    "Lattices: hex(side, Orient::Pointy | Orient::Flat), lattice::rect(pitch_u, pitch_v), staggered(pitch_u, pitch_v, shift), tri(side), along(&path, count, cell_poly). Then .rib(t) (walls t thick between cells), .at(origin), .turned(deg), and .cells(&region, min_area) -> Vec<Cell>: index [column, row], centre, region (the cell's material inside the region), clipped, poly(), area().",
    "Your own ingredients: an ingredient file in the library (ingredients/<name>.rs: //! ingredient: <name> header, then pub fns, types and consts, no main) is imported with use ingredients::<name>::*; (latest) or ingredients::<name>::v<N> (pinned). Inside one, reach another as crate::ingredients::<other>. It has the powers of the recipe that imports it, nothing more. Keep one from a run: nugget {action:\"save\", kind:\"ingredient\", from:\"<recipe name>\", items:[\"cells\"], title:\"honeycomb\"} lifts those items and what they use, made pub; it is kept only if it builds alone. Bring one from another library (release to beta, a colleague): nugget {action:\"save\", kind:\"ingredient\", from:\"<file>.rs\"} imports the kept file as it is, checked and built alone, marked imported; another ingredient of that name is kept beside it as <name>-2 unless replace:true. nugget {action:\"find\", query} finds them.",
    "Gears (API 1.12): use lime_recipe::gears::*; the library's involute-gears v1, adopted with the same names and the library's numbers bit for bit (its platform trig, so like the library copy the last bit can differ between lust and rustc): gear_outline(z, m, phase_deg), gear_outline_with(z, m, backlash, flank_points, phase_deg) (a polyline, 20 degrees), gear_tooth, pitch_radius(z, m), involute(a), mate_phase(own_phase_deg, own_z, dir_deg, mate_z), mate_turn(own_turn_deg, own_z, mate_z), dir_deg(a, b), idler_centre(a, c, d1, d2, left) -> Option<P2>, rack_outline(m, &centres, back). A plugin that imports ingredients::involute_gears keeps its own copy and builds as it did.",
