    "  The kernel builds the same outline as one step: ops::gear(\"fuse\", &gear, thickness, origin).set(\"bore\", 5.0) for model_apply, ops::gear_solid(&gear, thickness) for solid_new's gear (guide {kind:\"gear\"}). A gear train: let d = a.centre_distance(&b); let ph = mate_phase(0.0, a.teeth, 0.0, b.teeth); then ops::gear(\"fuse\", &b, 6.0, [d, 0.0, 0.0]).set(\"phaseDeg\", ph).",
    "Pendulums (API 1.13): use lime_recipe::mech::*; pendulum_period(length_mm) -> s and pendulum_length(period_s) -> mm for a simple pendulum, compound_period(inertia_g_mm2, mass_g, d_mm) -> s and equivalent_length(inertia_g_mm2, mass_g, d_mm) -> mm for a part on a hinge (model_mass {about:\"hinge\"} gives the inertia, mass and lever arm), G_MM_S2 = 9806.65. Small swings, no friction; lust and rustc give the same bits. A recipe can take the period as its parameter: let rod = pendulum_length(s.number(\"period\", 0.75).unit(\"s\").get());",
    "Clock ingredients (API 1.14): use lime_recipe::horology::*; pure functions, the same bits under lust and rustc, outlines as gears::Outline (to_loop() for extrude, outline_points(&o, step_deg) for a polyline).",
