    "  Shipped as plugins (nothing open needed, recipe_run {plugin}): clock-ratchet-wheel, clock-ratchet-click, clock-escape-wheel, clock-graham-anchor, clock-wheel-pinion; each stands its part with its axis or pivot at its own origin, the wheel on the model origin and the click, anchor or pinion where it belongs.",
    "  Cycloidal clock teeth (BS 978-2): ClockWheel::new(teeth, module, pinion_leaves) (epicycloidal addenda, practical addendum 0.95 f_a, dedendum pi/2 m; addendum_factor(), tip_radius(), root_radius(), centre_distance()), wheel.pinion(LeafTop::Round | Medium | High) -> ClockPinion (radial flanks, leaves 1.05 m or 1.25 m from 11 leaves). Mesh with gears::mate_phase(0.0, z, dir, leaves) as for involute gears.",
    "  Bores: pin_bore(pin_mm, Fit::Running | Sliding | Press, allowance_mm) (STEEL_PINS 1, 1.5, 2, 3), hole and shaft for any size to 30 mm, fit_clearance (ISO 286 H9/d9, H7/h6, H7/p6 means); bearing(\"623\") -> Bearing {bore, outer, width} with seat(fit, allowance) and shaft(fit, allowance); BEARINGS lists 608, 623 to 626, 683 to 685, 693 to 695 and MR63 to MR115. pin_bore, hole and shaft return Option<f64> (None outside 0 to 30 mm). pin_bore is the pin size plus the fit's clearance plus allowance_mm: the allowance is how much your printer makes a hole of that size undersize, so it is added to the drawn bore (positive when holes print small, usually tenths of a mm; shaft subtracts it, for a shaft that prints oversize), from a fit coupon. Press has a negative clearance (4 to 18 microns of interference) and Sliding a positive one (8 to 17 microns): an ISO press class differs from a sliding one by only 12 to 35 microns, below what a filament printer resolves, so a printed press fit needs its interference chosen by measurement (a coupon), not by the class.",
